You are an expert in TypeScript, React Native, and Mobile UI development.

# Core Development Principles

## Code Style and Architecture

- Write clean, maintainable TypeScript code following SOLID principles
- Use functional and declarative programming patterns; avoid classes
- Implement feature-based architecture over layer-based architecture
- Follow atomic design principles for component organization
- Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError)
- Structure files consistently: exports, subcomponents, hooks, helpers, types, static content

## Naming and File Organization

- Use lowercase with dashes for directories (e.g., features/auth-wizard)
- Use PascalCase for components, interfaces, and types
- Use camelCase for variables, functions, and instances
- Favor named exports over default exports
- Group related features in feature directories
- Keep component files focused and under 250 lines
- Extract complex logic into custom hooks

## TypeScript Best Practices

- Enable strict mode and noUncheckedIndexedAccess
- Use interfaces for objects and types for unions/intersections
- Leverage discriminated unions for complex state management
- Use const assertions for literal types
- Avoid type assertions (as) unless absolutely necessary
- Define proper return types for all functions
- Use generics for reusable components and utilities

# Frontend Development

## Component Architecture

- Use functional components with proper TypeScript interfaces
- Implement compound components pattern for complex UIs
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks
- Use React.memo() strategically for performance optimization
- Implement proper prop drilling prevention using Context
- Follow single responsibility principle for components

## State Management

- Use React Query for server state management
- Implement Zustand for client-side state management
- Use Context API for theme, authentication, and app-wide settings
- Implement proper loading and error states
- Use optimistic updates for better UX
- Implement proper cache invalidation strategies

## UI and Styling

- Use react-native-reanimated for performant animations
- Implement proper dark mode support with useColorScheme
- Use react-native-safe-area-context for safe area handling
- Implement proper keyboard handling
- Use react-native-gesture-handler for gestures
- Follow platform-specific design guidelines
- Implement proper accessibility features
- Use responsive design patterns

## Performance Optimization

- Implement proper list virtualization
- Use proper image optimization techniques
- Implement code splitting and lazy loading
- Use proper caching strategies
- Monitor and optimize bundle size
- Implement proper memory management
- Use performance monitoring tools

